id":"edexcel-as-p2-2025-jun-q4a","p":43,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4(a)","parentQuestion":"4","choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"In 2023 the UK government reduced indirect tax on certain goods and services. Define the term ‘indirect tax’.","topics":["2-6-2-demand-side-policies","1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1","theme-2"],"keywords":["indirect tax","definition"],"qpPage":8,"msPage":7,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p3-2025-jun-q2a","p":24,"section":"B","questionNumber":"2(a)","parentQuestion":"2","choiceGroup":null,"marks":5,"questionText":"Using a demand and supply diagram, explain the cost of a subsidy on the market for cooking oil to the Indian government (Extract E, line 6).","topics":["1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["subsidy","cost of a subsidy","demand and supply diagram","India"],"qpPage":16,"msPage":16,"ctxPage":33,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-as-p1-2024-jun-q6f","p":33,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(f)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":"edexcel-as-p1-2024-jun-q6-choice","marks":20,"questionText":"Evaluate the likely impact of a tax on plastic food-packaging. Use a diagram to support your answer.","topics":["1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["indirect tax","plastic packaging","tax incidence","diagram"],"qpPage":14,"msPage":19,"ctxPage":12,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2021-nov-q4b","p":7,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4(b)","parentQuestion":"4","choiceGroup":null,"marks":2,"questionText":"Patrick Street Productions produces musicals. Its latest production is ‘It’s a Wonderful Life’ and the total cost of this production is $200 000. The ticket price is $40. The theatre has a capacity of 300 seats. The company aims for revenue maximisation. If this is achieved, revenue from ticket sales will cover 30% of total costs. Charitable donations contribute 12.5% towards total cost and a government subsidy ensures the production covers all of its costs. Calculate the value of the government subsidy necessary for this production to cover all of its costs.","topics":["3-3-2-costs","1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1","theme-3"],"keywords":["subsidy","total costs","calculation","theatre"],"qpPage":9,"msPage":9,"ctxPage":8,"modelAnswer":null,"ctxLabel":"Question 4 as printed"},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2021-nov-q6d","p":7,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(d)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":12,"questionText":"With reference to Extract C, discuss the proposed government subsidy to prevent Thomas Cook from reaching its shut-down point.","topics":["3-3-4-normal-profits-supernormal-profits-losses","1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1","theme-3"],"keywords":["shut-down point","subsidy","losses","Thomas Cook"],"qpPage":16,"msPage":16,"ctxPage":14,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2020-oct-q1a","p":8,"section":"A","questionNumber":"1(a)","parentQuestion":"1","choiceGroup":null,"marks":4,"questionText":"Fuel duty is an excise tax imposed on the sale of petrol, included in the price paid by consumers, set at 58 pence per litre. Draw a supply and demand diagram to show the incidence of a specific petrol tax on consumers and producers.","topics":["1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["indirect tax","tax incidence","specific tax","petrol"],"qpPage":2,"msPage":4,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-as-p1-2020-oct-q3b","p":35,"section":"A","questionNumber":"3(b)","parentQuestion":"3","choiceGroup":null,"marks":3,"questionText":"The ‘Energy Company Obligation’ is the government’s term for its programme to make houses in the UK more energy efficient. Explain an opportunity cost to the government of granting subsidies to energy suppliers to install loft insulation.","topics":["1-1-3-the-economic-problem","1-2-9-in